import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { repo } from '../lib/projects';
---
<Layout title="About the archive — Killed by Tesla"><main id="main" class="record"><a class="back" href="/">← Back to project index</a><div class="eyebrow">ABOUT / METHODOLOGY</div><h1>A public record<span class="red">.</span></h1><div class="prose"><p class="record-summary">An independent, community-maintained archive of Tesla’s ended projects and announced wind-downs.</p><h2>What belongs here</h2><p>Discontinued products, cancelled projects, ended programs, and announced production wind-downs. Ordinary model-year changes and unsupported speculation are excluded. Acquired businesses may appear for historical context, with their origins and acquisition clearly stated.</p><h2>How to read a status</h2><dl class="definitions"><dt>Discontinued</dt><dd>A released product or operating program has ended. Remaining inventory or support may continue.</dd><dt>Cancelled</dt><dd>An announced project was ended before customer delivery.</dd><dt>Announced wind-down</dt><dd>A future ending or factory wind-down has been announced. It is not counted as an already ended project, and does not automatically mean global discontinuation.</dd><dt>Absorbed brand</dt><dd>A business or brand integrated into Tesla. It is excluded from the ended-project count.</dd></dl><h2>Dates and evidence</h2><p>Dates use only the precision supported by sources. Released products start with customer availability; cancelled projects start with announcement. Production completion, withdrawal from sale, and brand acquisition are different events, explained in each record. Planned dates never change a status automatically.</p><p>Every entry links to evidence for its start and ending, preferring company statements and filings, followed by reputable reporting. “Last verified” records the most recent source review, not a claim of continuous monitoring. This is a maintained archive, not an exhaustive list.</p><h2>Contribute</h2><p><a href={`${repo}/issues/new/choose`}>Suggest an entry or correction</a> with a source link, or edit an entry’s YAML file on GitHub and open a pull request. No local development setup is required for data changes. Read the <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md`}>contribution guide</a> for examples.</p><h2>Open source and independent</h2><p>Inspired by <a href="https://killedbygoogle.com/">Killed by Google</a>. This project is not affiliated with Tesla, Inc. Product names identify the projects being documented. Code is licensed under MIT; original archive text and data under CC BY 4.0. Linked sources retain their own rights.</p></div></main></Layout>
